Description: Move a cue's edge only where that takes quiet away
 A cue's end was moved to the end of the last stretch of speech that lay mostly
 inside it. A cue whose text went on after a pause, in speech that ran on into
 the next cue, was so cut at that pause, and a cue that began inside the
 speech of the cue before it lost its first words the same way. An edge now
 moves to the edge of the cue's own speech only when the edge word reaches into
 it, or when nothing sounds between it and that word. Clicks and breaths
 shorter than 80 ms between two sentences no longer join their speech into one
 stretch.
